{#-
  The archived-versions table of contents (Stage 6d, design.md section 10.6).

  Flat, like `documents_toc.yml.j2` and for the same reason -- a history is a
  list. The keys differ from that one because the items are not files: `version`
  is the catalog's string and never parsed out of a ZIP filename (19% of those
  carry a former product name), `released` is the month or empty, and `available`
  says whether `path` can be fetched from this tree at all.

  `bytes` is written only for a ZIP that was actually copied in; a remote one's
  size is not something this tool has measured, and publishing a 0 would read as
  an empty file rather than as an unknown.

  `entries` arrives ordered from `sync/archives.py` -- version descending, the
  non-numeric strings last. Nothing is sorted here.

  The two optional keys are written with the `{% raw %}{% if %}{% endraw %}` opening the
  *same* line as the key rather than the line above it. A block tag on its own line
  keeps the newline before it and swallows the two-space indent after it, which
  emits `path:` at column 0 -- still YAML, and silently a sibling of `items`
  rather than a member of the entry.
-#}
# AEM table of contents{% if title %} for {{ title }}{% endif %}
# Generated by DocuShift (Stage 6) -- do not edit by hand.
items:
{% for entry in entries -%}
- version: {{ entry.version | yaml }}
  released: {{ entry.released | yaml }}
  available: {{ 'true' if entry.available else 'false' }}
{% if entry.url %}  path: {{ entry.url | yaml }}
{% endif %}{% if entry.bytes %}  bytes: {{ entry.bytes }}
{% endif %}{% endfor -%}
